<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gives states $3.6 bln to make up tax loss.</title>
<headline>Brazil gives states $3.6 bln to make up tax loss.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian President Fernando Henrique Cardoso on Wednesday signed a bill transferring 3.6 billion reais to the states and municipalities to compensate them for losses on export taxes, officials said.</p>
<p>The money was part of a deal struck in Congress for the approval of a bill exempting primary and intermediate goods from so-called ICMS export tax.</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
